  "strings": {
    "Add Another Account…": {},
    "Add Google Account…": {},
    "All your Google calendars as one. Edits open in Google Calendar.": {},
    "Calendars": {},
    "Cancel": {},
    "Choose Calendars…": {},
    "Day": {},
    "Day reads your calendars from Google and keeps them on your devices. Your sign-in moves between them in iCloud Keychain, which is end-to-end encrypted. To pick up changes sooner, Google tells Day's server at apps.idea2prod.in that a calendar changed, never what changed. What the server keeps about your devices is in Day's [privacy policy](https://apps.idea2prod.in/day/privacy.html).": {},
    "Day reads your calendars from Google and keeps them on your devices. Your sign-in moves between them in iCloud Keychain, which is end-to-end encrypted. To pick up changes sooner, Google tells Day's server at apps.idea2prod.in that a calendar changed, never what changed. What the server keeps about your devices is in Day's [privacy policy](https://apps.idea2prod.in/day/privacy.html). On the Mac, Day also checks for updates through apps.idea2prod.in, which counts checks and downloads by app, version and country and never stores your IP address.": {},
    "Day signs it out on your Mac and iPhone and deletes its saved events.": {},
